{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And on the seventh day He ceased and rested.</b> Rabbi Yehudah HaChasid says that from here there is a hint to the additional soul on the Sabbath: take the final letters of these words and they total two. (Tanchuma, parashat zo.) And there is an account of Turnus Rufus the wicked who encountered Rabbi Akiva on the Sabbath. He said to him: What is this day different from other days? He said to him: What is this man different from other men? He said to him: What did I say to you and what did you say to me, etc.? What is the Sabbath different from the other days — and I said to you: what makes you different from other people? He said to him: דמרי צבי — that is, 'Because my Master [HaShem] desired it,' that they honor me for making me king. He said to him: So too the Sabbath — the Holy One, blessed be He, desired it, that it be honored. He said to him: Then why does He perform labor in it — moving from domain to domain, spirits and rains? He said to him: I know of you that you are expert in the Torah of the Jews: if two dwell in one courtyard, and this one establishes an eruv and that one establishes an eruv, perhaps they are permitted to carry on the Sabbath; but if one man dwells in one large courtyard, even as large as Antioch, he is permitted to carry throughout all of it. And the Holy One, blessed be He — the heavens are His throne and the earth is His footstool, and the whole earth is full of His glory, and all is His. Therefore He may carry throughout the entire world."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:29.052910861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}